Cell["\<\
This is a feature of Mathematica: by default, if we assign a value without \
decimal point, it is a whole number (integral or rational). With the decimal \
point, it is a real number with \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]floating point\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. What is a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]floating point\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] number? we will learn about this later. For now, \
just think of it as a real number.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7558622739594727`*^9, 3.755862467828051*^9}, {
  3.7558643090219297`*^9, 
  3.7558643213627796`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"63f10eda-f1c2-4acf-aa49-\
3fe5bc1aea56"],

